<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Desire for God" cic="CCC 27-30, 44-45" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in groups. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Recalling the essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What is the phrase from St. Augustine that opens the lesson? What does it mean?</li>
<li>Explain in your own words Fulton Sheen's image of the «God-shaped hole».</li>
<li>What does the Catechism mean when it states that man is «capable» of God (CCC 27)?</li>
<li>What are the two opposite errors about faith that the lesson points out?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For reflection and writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question sincerely. There are no «correct» answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What things do you seek to feel happy? (friends, success, rest, screens...)</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Make a list of 5 things you turn to when you feel empty or lonely.</p>
<p class="question-block__p" style="margin-top:8px">___________ ___________ ___________ ___________ ___________</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Has any of those things given you happiness that lasts forever?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">If the answer is no, why do you think we keep looking in the same places?</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Of the seven obstacles to recognizing God (CCC 29), which seems most common in your environment?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">(Rebellion against evil, ignorance, indifference, riches/cares, bad example, hostile currents, sin)</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Have you ever felt that «something more» that you can't quite identify?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Describe the situation: When? Where? What were you doing?</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. What person in your life has helped you seek truth or ask important questions?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">The Catechism says that «man needs the witness of others who teach him to seek God» (CCC 30). Who has been that witness for you?</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical activities</h3>

<h4>A. The map of the heart</h4>
<p>Draw a large heart on a sheet of paper. Divide the heart into sections like puzzle pieces. In each section, write something that occupies space in your heart: your family, your friends, your dreams, your fears, your hobbies... Leave one section empty, unfilled. That section is the «God-shaped hole». Reflect: What are you putting there that isn't God? What would happen if you let God occupy that space?</p>

<h4>B. Psalm 42 in first person</h4>
<p>Read Psalm 42 slowly. Then write it in your own words, as if you were the one saying to God:</p>
<p style="border:1px dashed var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:16px;margin:12px 0;color:var(--text-soft);font-style:italic">«As the deer longs for water, so my soul longs for you, my God...»</p>
<p><em>Continue your personal version of the psalm (4-6 lines):</em></p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Dialogue with Fulton Sheen</h4>
<p>Imagine you can talk with Venerable Fulton Sheen. He tells you that you have a God-shaped hole in your soul. What do you respond? Write a brief dialogue (10-12 lines) between you and him.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
